## Session Model

The pipeline runs in a single conversation by default. Agent Teams
teammates are spawned within the same lead session, each with their
own context window. Context management uses a living pipeline
snapshot plus two model-aware absolute token thresholds (not
percentages). See SKILL.md Rule 10 for the authoritative snapshot
structure and handoff protocol.

**Context thresholds** (model-aware absolute token counts):

<!-- {context_thresholds}: Populated by /ai-dlc-setup Step 2 from
     the selected model strategy. Defaults per SKILL.md Rule 10:
     200K model → yellow 80K, red 120K; 1M model → yellow 120K,
     red 200K. -->

{context_thresholds}

**Yellow-threshold reminder.** When conversation context first
crosses the yellow threshold, the agent outputs a one-line reminder
with three routed options: (1) new session via handoff (recommended
before any gate or deployment), (2) `/compact` (acceptable only
mid-step), (3) continue (only if the current sub-step is about to
wrap). Non-blocking.

**Red-threshold reminder.** When conversation context first crosses
the red threshold, the agent outputs an urgent one-line reminder:
degradation is likely present; strongly recommend new session at the
next sub-step boundary; avoid `/compact` before any gate,
deployment, or adversarial review. Non-blocking — the user's
judgment is authoritative.

**Recurring reminders.** Past the yellow threshold, the yellow
reminder re-fires every additional 50K tokens OR every 20 turns
(whichever comes first). Same pattern past the red threshold.

**Context introspection — user is source of truth.** The agent
cannot reliably self-measure its own context window. Two modes apply.

**Mode 1 — user-shared `/context` (authoritative).** The most recent
user-shared `/context` output drives both the threshold-crossing
check AND the recurrence arithmetic. When a crossing fires under
Mode 1, the agent emits the full Rule 10 reminder and advances
`last_yellow_fire_*` / `last_red_fire_*` in the snapshot. The agent
MAY invite the user to share `/context` at any point.

**Mode 2 — fallback estimate (advisory only).** When no user-shared
`/context` is available, the agent computes:

```
estimate = 15,000  (baseline for CLAUDE.md + skill + system prompt)
        + (turns_this_session * 2,000)  (approx per-exchange cost)
        + sum(tool_output_sizes_in_bytes) * 0.25  (bytes-to-tokens conservative high)
```

If the estimate crosses a threshold, the agent does NOT emit the
full Rule 10 reminder. It emits this lighter check-line instead:

> *"Context estimate suggests crossing the {yellow|red} threshold
> (~{estimate}K tokens, fallback heuristic). Please share
> `/context` output to confirm. I will continue with this estimate
> as a working assumption until confirmed."*

Under Mode 2, recurrence arithmetic is NOT advanced — the
`last_yellow_fire_*` / `last_red_fire_*` snapshot fields only update
when a user-shared `/context` confirms the crossing. This prevents
noisy re-firing of unverified estimates. When the user responds
with `/context` output, the agent treats the shared value as Mode 1
input.

**Human-requested handoff.** When the user requests handoff, the
agent commits in-flight work, finalizes the snapshot, outputs a
pasteable resume prompt pointing at the snapshot, and ends the
session. The new conversation resumes from the snapshot.

**Auto-handoff mode.** A configurable setting controls whether the
lead MAY automatically execute the Rule 10(a) handoff procedure
when the red threshold has been confirmed crossed at a safe seam.

<!-- {auto_handoff_mode}: Populated by /ai-dlc-setup Step 2. One of
     `off`, `deploy-only`, or `safe-seam`. Defaults: new installs
     use `safe-seam`; upgrades from a pre-feature install default
     to `off`. -->

```
auto_handoff_mode: {auto_handoff_mode}
```

Mode semantics:

- `off` — Auto-handoff MUST NOT fire at any seam. Yellow and red
  reminders remain non-blocking; the user decides when to handoff.
- `deploy-only` — Auto-handoff MAY fire only at the
  `deploy-validate.md` Step 0 pre-flight context check when that
  check cannot otherwise be satisfied.
- `safe-seam` — Auto-handoff MAY fire at every safe seam defined
  in `gate-validation.md` "Auto-handoff evaluation" (Seam A deploy
  pre-flight, Seam B end-of-step before gate validation, Seam C
  story transitions, Seam D between adversarial passes) when all
  preconditions are met.

Every seam is an EVALUATION point. Evaluation fires handoff ONLY
when ALL of these preconditions hold:

1. `auto_handoff_mode` permits firing at this seam.
2. `context_reminders_sent: red` in the snapshot (red threshold
   confirmed crossed under Mode 1 via user-shared `/context`).
   Mode 2 fallback estimates MUST NOT fire auto-handoff.
3. Snapshot is current: either `gate-validation.md` Check 15 passed
   on the most recent gate, or the sub-step snapshot update just
   refreshed the snapshot successfully.
4. No gate validation is currently executing.
5. No deployment is currently executing.
6. No teammate is awaiting a lead orchestration response.
7. No pending user directive awaits response (lead is not at any
   pause point in SKILL.md Rule 7).

Auto-handoff execution follows the Rule 10(a) 4-step procedure
without modification. Auto-handoff is NOT an additional pause
point — it is a session-terminating action.

Auto-handoff output MUST be distinguishable from a human-requested
handoff. The lead outputs this line immediately before the Rule 10
resume prompt:

> *"Auto-handoff triggered by auto_handoff_mode=<mode> at
> <seam_name>. Context at <tokens> tokens, red threshold confirmed
> via user-shared /context."*

The agent does NOT force handoff at any context threshold under
`auto_handoff_mode: off`.

